  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing UI Components**\n\nOkay, I\'m diving into the UI components now. Specifically, I\'m starting with `components/CommonComponents.kt`. The first component I\'m focusing on is `HeaderCard`. It\'s going to be an elegant gradient banner to display the total uncollected cash with a quick summary.\n\n\n**Defining UI Elements**\n\nNow, I\'m fleshing out the UI elements. Specifically, I\'m thinking about components like `MetricPill` for key figures and badges, and `SectionTitle` with typography and an action button. I\'m also planning for `CurrencyFormattedText`, `ProgressBar`, `CategoryChip`, and the `AppBottomNavigation` with all its icons. Next, I am thinking about the screens and their components. I\'m imagining a `DashboardScreen.kt`, focusing on top summaries and the \"Windfall Splitter Simulator\". Finally I have a concept for \"Actionable Collection Alerts\"\n\n\n**Expanding Screen Features**\n\nI am now focusing on refining the screens and adding detailed features. Specifically, `FreelanceCollectorScreen.kt` will have project lists with filter tabs, and add/edit dialogs. A \"Collect Money Dialog\" with auto-allocation options and a \"Send Payment Reminder Sheet\" with pre-formatted templates is included. Meanwhile, `HouseholdBudgetScreen.kt` will have a visual balance chart, expense lists, and payer allocation settings. I am also planning indicators for monthly living runway and cash surplus.\n\n\n**Developing Financial Views**\n\nI\'ve moved on to designing more financial views. I\'m thinking through `BankDebtScreen.kt` with payoff strategies and a timeline projector, plus a quick \"Extra Payoff\" button.  Also, I\'m sketching out `SavingsTargetsScreen.kt` with accumulator cards, milestones, and quick deposit functionality. Finally, I\'m conceptualizing an `AiAdvisorScreen.kt`, powered by Gemini, for personalized financial advice.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 6
      nanos: 909410914
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
